  "title": "Forge seam: provider-neutral interface, GitHub adapter, in-memory double",
  "summary": "This change introduces a provider-neutral `Forge` trait as the seam between the factory and a code host, and moves the existing `gh`-driving code behind it. A new `forge` module defines the trait, its request/response types and a `report_change` step that opens a pull request, writes the status block, checks capabilities, posts the review and reads check status in one fixed order. A new `github` module is the first adapter, wrapping the existing `GhClient` and review/pr_status helpers; `pr_status` and `review` are stripped of their process-spawning code and reduced to pure parsing/decision functions. An in-memory `FakeForge` records every call and can script answers or failures, letting a full run be exercised with no process, file, network or clock. `main.rs` is rewired so `review post`, `review run --post-to`, `pr status apply` and `pr status refresh` all go through the forge.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
